            <ArticleTitle>Testing for cardiac markers at the point of care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>351-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Measurement of cardiac markers at the point of care is feasible, diagnostically accurate, and, when combined with appropriate decision-making algorithms, cost effective. It may be the only way to deliver results rapidly enough for therapeutic intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
